    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>For Admin, partner, manager and staff IDs</b></p>


<p>1.If an Attendance is created after promotion/rejoining → Show new staff code, new role, new joining date.<br/>
2.If an Attendance is created (before promotion/rejoining) → Show old staff code, old role, old joining date.</p>

<ol>
	<li>Check that for existing user, staff code, role &amp; joining date will be same based on date of joining.</li>
	<li>Check that for existing user who re-joined after leaving, at the date of rejoined, or at the time of attendance generation in the attendance module; a) name will get added b) New staff code will be shown c) If user has joined to upper position, then new role will be shown in attendance. d) New rejoined date will be also shown in attendance.</li>
</ol>

            <br/>
        </td>
