    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>For Partner, Manager, Staff,  Promoted User and Rejoined User Ids</b><br/>
<b>Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Human Resources' dropdown.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Timesheet' dropdown and navigate to 'My Timesheet'.</li>
	<li>Click on 'Add Timesheet'.</li>
</ol>


<p>1.Fill timesheet in bulk for one full week and save the data successfully. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>2.Fill multiple timesheets after change 'to date' and ensure all are saved properly. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>3.Apply casual leave on a Monday – check if both the "From Date" and "To Date" are showing correctly. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>4.Apply casual leave for two separate days within a week – ensure both "From Date" and "To Date" are accurate. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>5.Apply exam leave on a Monday (Approved/Rejected) – verify the accuracy of the "From Date" and "To Date". - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>6.Apply exam leave for two separate days in a week (Approved/Rejected) – verify the accuracy of the "From Date" and "To Date". - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>7.Partners and Managers can select Off/Holiday client only on 2nd &amp; 4th Saturdays and official holidays. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>8.Staff can select Off/Holiday client on all Saturdays and official holidays. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>9.A maximum of 4 fields can be added per section. User should also be able to remove fields. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>10.User cannot change the ‘From Date’; only the ‘To Date’ will be change. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>11.If user selects 2 days while filling timesheet, then only 2 days' data can be saved. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>12.Reject 2nd and 4th Saturday timesheets for Partner/Manager in which rejected timesheet should not be off/holidays client . - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>13.When creating a child field, all fields inside the child field must be mandatory. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>14.Check date sequence to ensure days are ordered like 1, 2, 3, etc. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>15.User cannot select Off/Holiday client from child fields. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>16.All mandatory fields must be filled before submission. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>17.The Hour field should accept only digits (no text). - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>18.User cannot fill timesheets for future dates. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>19.Total hours cannot exceed 12 in any section. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>20.When a child field is removed, the total hours should automatically decrease based on the removed entry. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>21.If a user selects 4 days but fills data for only 2 days, submission should be restricted (all selected days are mandatory). (related to child task) - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p><a href="http://22.By" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">22</a>.  by default, timesheet for 7 days (1 week) should be displayed if user did not save 1 week timesheet on that case. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>23.If a user has applied for casual leave on a particular date, that date should not appear while filling the timesheet. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>24.If a user has applied for exam leave and it is approved, the leave date should not appear during timesheet filling. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>25.Auto-fill timesheet for 1st to 5th Saturdays for staff only. when user select off/holidays client. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>26.Auto-fill timesheet for 2nd and 4th Saturdays for managers and partners only. when user select off/holidays client. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>27.Total hours should be updated on assignment as the timesheet is saved. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>28.If a user joins between Monday and Saturday, system should allow accurate date handling. - <b>Pass</b></p>

<p>29.Auto-fill for official holiday dates should be available. when user select off/holidays client.</p>

<p>30. If a user selects an Off/Holiday client in any main field, then: - <b>Pass</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><b>All child fields</b> under that main field should be <b>automatically removed and</b></li>
	<li>The <b>total hour</b> should be <b>recalculated</b> accordingly</li>
</ul>


<ol>
	<li>When a user selects an off/holiday client, the hours will automatically be set to 0, and in this case, no validation will be triggered for the hour field upon submission. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>When a user selects any client other than an off/holiday client, hour validation will be triggered during submission to ensure that appropriate hours are entered. - <b>Pass</b></li>
</ol>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

