    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><a href="https://capitallio.atlassian.net/browse/VS-312" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://capitallio.atlassian.net/browse/VS-312</a> </p>

<p><b>For Admin IDs</b></p>

<p><b>Steps: 1</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Dashboard'.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Team Member Box'.</li>
	<li>Go to the status column</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Steps: 2</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Dashboard'.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Team Member Box'.</li>
	<li>Click on the Team Member Name hyperlink.</li>
	<li>Go to the status field</li>
	<li>click on acive/inactive button</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Steps : 3</b><br/>
If a user is rejoined and does not have a leaving date for rejoining, the admin can activate or deactivate the user. However, if the rejoined user has a leaving date after rejoining, the admin cannot activate or deactivate them.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <br/>

    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
