    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <ol>
	<li>If a timesheet is submitted on Saturday, the date will be enabled the following Monday. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>If a timesheet is submitted on Sunday, the date will be enabled the following Monday. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>When a user saves timesheet data, the next day's date will be displayed - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>If casual leave is applied immediately after submitting the timesheet, the date will be displayed after the leave's end date. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>If exam leave is applied immediately after submitting the timesheet, the date will be displayed after the leave's end date. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>When casual leave is applied and there is a gap between the saved timesheet date and the casual leave start date, the date will be displayed after the saved timesheet date. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>When exam leave is applied and there is a gap between the saved timesheet date and the exam leave start date, the date will be displayed after the saved timesheet date. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>If you are not working on Sunday and want the date to be enabled on Monday, you must submit the timesheet for that week. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>If a date is enabled in the future and the user tries to submit their timesheet, they will not be able to submit it. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>If a user submits a timesheet for the current date, future dates will not be enabled. This applies only to saved timesheets. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>Apply Multiple leave - user can apply multiple leaves and date gets enabled accordingly - <b>Pass VSA 408</b></li>
	<li><b>New Joiner Case</b></li>
</ol>


<ul>
	<li>If a user is a new joiner, their date will be enabled on their joining date &amp; if date falls in between the week then previous date data will get created as ’N/A' automatically on first day timesheet created. - <b>Pass</b></li>
	<li>After that all previous test cases will apply. - <b>Pass</b></li>
</ul>


<ol>
	<li><b>After Rejoining (Same Post or Different Post)</b></li>
</ol>


<ul>
	<li>If a user rejoins, their date will be enabled on their rejoining date.</li>
	<li>After that all previous test cases will apply</li>
</ul>


<p><b>For Partner, Manager, and Staff IDs</b><br/>
<b>Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Human Resources' dropdown.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Timesheet' dropdown and navigate to 'My Timesheet'.</li>
	<li>Click on 'Add Timesheet'.</li>
</ol>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <br/>

