    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Inactive Assignments for Users</b></p>

<p>Ensure assignments do not appear for users after being marked inactive for that assignment.</p>

<p><b>For Admin ID</b></p>

<p><b>Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on <b>'View All Assignments'</b> in the <b>Assignment Section</b>.</li>
	<li>Click on the <b>Assignment ID hyperlink</b>.</li>
	<li>Go to the <b>Teammember List</b> section.
	<ul>
		<li>Here, you can see the <b>Active/Inactive</b> button.</li>
		<li>Now admin can do <b>Active/Inactive</b> &amp; check to respective logins.</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ol>


<p><b>For Manager and Staff IDs</b></p>

<p><b>Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the <b>'Dashboard'</b>.</li>
	<li>Click on the <b>'Open Assignment Box'</b>.
	<ul>
		<li>Inactive assignments will be hidden.</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Additional Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the <b>'Dashboard</b>.</li>
</ol>


<p>Inactive assignments will be hidden in Assignment Section</p>

<p> </p>

<p><b>Alternative Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the <b>'Client'</b> dropdown.</li>
	<li>Navigate to the <b>'Assignment List'</b> page.</li>
	<li>Click on the <b>Client Name hyperlink</b> and click on year.</li>
</ol>


<p>Inactive assignments will be hidden.</p>

<p> </p>

<p><b>Manager-Specific Tab</b></p>

<p>This tab is available <b>only for managers</b> and not for staff.</p>

<p><b>Steps:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the <b>'Client'</b> dropdown.</li>
	<li>Navigate to the <b>'Client List'</b> page.</li>
	<li>Click on the <b>Client Name hyperlink</b> and select <b>Assignment</b>.</li>
</ol>


<p>       Inactive assignments will be hidden.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

