    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Test cases:-</p>

<ol>
	<li>If user will submit 2 week timesheet and admin rejected the timesheet continuously till first week's Saturday only then user will be able to apply leave on Sunday in first week but not on second week’s Sunday.</li>
	<li>If continuous dates were not rejected till Sunday then user will not able to apply leave on Sunday.</li>
	<li>If user fill and submits the timesheet from e.g*. Monday to Sunday* and will try to apply leave on <b>Sunday</b> and <b>Saturday to Sunday</b> timesheet will not rejected then user will not able to proceed it</li>
	<li>If partner and manager will submits the timesheet from <b>Monday to Saturday</b> and again from <b>Monday to Saturday</b> and if partner and manager will try to apply leave on <b>upcoming Sunday</b> in each weeks then regarding leave status will be visible in attendance (CL and EL)</li>
	<li>If staff will submits the timesheet from Monday to Friday and admin will reject the timesheet from <b>Monday to Friday</b> then staff can apply leave on <b>Saturday on Sunday.</b></li>
	<li>If staff will submits the timesheet from <b>Monday to Sunday</b> admin will only reject the timesheet till <b>Monday to Friday</b> and not on Saturday and Sunday then staff will not be able to apply leave on <b>Saturday and Sunday.</b></li>
</ol>


<p><a href="https://capitallio.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A3bb006a3-fefb-46cb-bba3-303693cb0c73" class="user-hover" rel="712020:3bb006a3-fefb-46cb-bba3-303693cb0c73" data-account-id="712020:3bb006a3-fefb-46cb-bba3-303693cb0c73" accountid="712020:3bb006a3-fefb-46cb-bba3-303693cb0c73" rel="noreferrer">Shahid Raza</a>  Kindly review it and share your updates.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <br/>

