    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>These are old points and no required for testing</b></p>

<p>when user will rejoin manager to partner after that all previous data will be show according manager and current data will be show according partner.</p>



<p>when user rejoin on same post then nothing will be change only check below point </p>

<p>1.user can save timesheet without timesheet request send</p>

<p>2.user can not fill timesheet before rejoining date </p>



<p>Steps:-<br/>
1.Navigate to the application.<br/>
2.Click on '<tt>Permotion/Rejoining</tt>' dropdown.</p>

<p>3.Click on '<tt>rejoining detals button</tt>'<br/>
4.fill all data and click on submit button</p>

<p>Rejoining &amp; Promotion Process</p>

<ol>
	<li>In case of rejoining, “Rejoining date” is to be entered.</li>
	<li>If the designation of the rejoined individual is same, then the Employee code should remain same.</li>
	<li>In case there is change in designation, then the employee will be assigned a  new code.</li>
	<li>The new code should be linked to the old code and all the previous data will be accessible with the use of previous employee code and employee name.</li>
	<li>In case of change in code, new code should be mentioned on the profile of employee.</li>
	<li>In case of change in code, previous code should be mentioned on the team list with new staff code</li>
	<li>In case there is a change in designation, but the individual is mapped to a particular assignment then his right related to that assignment should not change till the assignment is over.</li>
	<li>Similar process to be carried out in case of Promotion of an employee from manager to partner.</li>
	<li>"The employee code will be shown according to the new assignment and previous assignment. The new employee code will be displayed everywhere except for the new and previous assignments, if the designation has changed."</li>
</ol>




<p><b>These are new points and required for testing</b></p>


<p><b>Steps to Navigate:</b><br/>
Use Admin IDs to promote or rejoin a user</p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the application.</li>
	<li>Click on the 'Promotion/Rejoining' tab.</li>
</ol>


<p><font color="#bf2600">After promoting or rejoining a user, we need to test all the points mentioned below</font></p>

<p><b>Promoted User (staff and manager) and Rejoined User (All  role) Ids;</b></p>

<p><b>1.If User rejoined with same role, same staff code will be displayed</b></p>

<p><b>2.If User rejoined on promoted role or ongoing user got promoted, promoted staff code will be displayed -</b> </p>

<ul>
	<li>Pass</li>
</ul>


<p><b>3.Assignment, Assignment related All data like saved timesheet, submitted timesheet, rejected timesheet etc:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>If a new assignment is created after promotion/rejoining → Show new staff code. - Pass</li>
	<li>If an old assignment (created before promotion/rejoining) → Show old staff code. - Pass</li>
</ul>




<p><b>2.Apply Leave, Timesheet Request &amp; Leave Request:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Requests made before rejoining/promotion → Old staff code should be displayed.</li>
	<li>Requests made after rejoining/promotion → New staff code should be displayed.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>3.we have to test on report, client/assignment, team , Promotion/Rejoining and Human Resources tab,</b></p>

<p><b>4.We need to test all dropdown fields where the staff code appears in case of promotion and rejoining</b></p>

<p><b>5.we have to test all section on dashboard,</b></p>

<p><b>6.I need to discuss three clients: Off/Holidays, Official Travel, Unallocated. and apply leave Currently, when you fill the timesheet for any of these clients, the old code is still appearing</b></p>



<p><a href="https://capitallio.atlassian.net/browse/VS-290" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://capitallio.atlassian.net/browse/VS-290</a> </p>

<p><a href="https://capitallio.atlassian.net/browse/VS-148" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://capitallio.atlassian.net/browse/VS-148</a> </p>

