    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>when user will promote manager to partner after that all previous data will be show according manager and current data will be show according partner.</p>

<p>Steps:-<br/>
1.Navigate to the application.<br/>
2.Click on '<tt>Promotion/Rejoining</tt>' dropdown.<br/>
3.fill all data and click on submit button</p>

<p>4.create new client and then create client for promotion user</p>



<p>Rejoining &amp; Promotion Process</p>

<ol>
	<li>In case of rejoining, “Rejoining date” is to be entered.</li>
	<li>If the designation of the rejoined individual is same, then the Employee code should remain same.</li>
	<li>In case there is change in designation, then the employee will be assigned a  new code.</li>
	<li>The new code should be linked to the old code and all the previous data will be accessible with the use of previous employee code and employee name.</li>
	<li>In case of change in code, previous code should be mentioned on the profile of employee.</li>
	<li>In case there is a change in designation, but the individual is mapped to a particular assignment then his right related to that assignment should not change till the assignment is over.</li>
	<li>Similar process to be carried out in case of Promotion of an employee from manager to partner.</li>
</ol>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <br/>

    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
