    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p> 1.By clicking on “No”, the user will be directed to another page where user will have to updated 3 things “Amount” (Compulsory), “Remarks” (Optional) and “Attachment” (Optional)</p>

<p>2..If “Pending”: - Option for follow up is there in the “Status” column against the pending responder.</p>

<p>3.Then the user can close it or save it as a draft or send it to the Responders.</p>

<p>4.After the user send it the page will be updated with the mail delivery status either “Sent” or “Failed”.</p>

<p>5.Responder will receive a mail with the mail body as updated by Organisation.</p>

<p>6. There will be a link in the mail, the Responder will click on the link, it will take him to a new browser page.</p>

<p>7.In case user “Accept” it: - By clicking on “Accept”, the user will be directed to confirmation page displaying the message “Your response has been recorded. Thank you”</p>

<p>8. If “Submit”: - By clicking on “Accept”, the user will be directed to confirmation page displaying the message “Your response has been recorded. Thank you”</p>

<p>9. In either case there will be a alert, “Are you sure”, before submission of any of the above response.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

